lua-async
=========

The lua-async package is an asynchronous executor for Lua. It makes blocking
libraries non-blocking using LuaLanes for OS worker threads and libuv for
the event loop.

Quick Start
-----------

* Report an issue: https://github.com/KushanWaghmare/lua-async/issues
* Get the latest release: https://github.com/KushanWaghmare/lua-async/releases
* Source repository: https://github.com/KushanWaghmare/lua-async
* Install package: luarocks install lua-async

Essential Documentation
-----------------------

All users should be familiar with:

* Execution Model:
  - Scheduler: Registers calling coroutines and non-blocking yields (async/scheduler.lua)
  - Pool: Multi-threaded lane management and Linda FIFO task queues (async/pool.lua)
  - Event Loop: 1ms timer dispatcher running on libuv (async/init.lua)

* Driver Adapters:
  - LuaSQL Adapter: Thread-safe connection pool with cursor drain (async/drivers/luasql.lua)
  - Redis Adapter: Non-blocking client wrapper (async/drivers/redis.lua)

* Driver Interface Specification:
  - setup(config) -> state: Initialises one connection per OS worker thread
  - call(state, method, args) -> result: Executes job inside thread and serialises output
  - teardown(state): Releases connections on pool shutdown

* Requirements:
  - Lua 5.1, 5.2, 5.3, 5.4, or LuaJIT
  - LuaLanes
  - luv (libuv)

